            "body": "@ngortheone these are for snippet placeholders from the lsp which mini.completion does not support yet.\r\n\r\nSee here for same issue on TypeScript and Lua and how to fixed it (assume similar setting for Go LSP but I have no Go experience): \r\n\r\n- https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/193#issuecomment-2017435585\r\n- https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/193#issuecomment-2028049110\r\n\r\nThe key is to try and find something in the Go LSP config/settings similar to this: `Lua.completion.callSnippet = 'Replace'`\r\n\r\nSee here for conversation on future mini.snippets being a module (WIP but nothing available yet): https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/886#issuecomment-2390989574",
