            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Judging by your dotfiles, you use 'nvim-lspconfig'. In that case I'd suggest passing it directly to the `require('lspconfig').gopls.setup()` with something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('lspconfig').gopls.setup({\r\n  capabilities = {\r\n    textDocument = {\r\n      completion = {\r\n        completionItem = {\r\n          snippetSupport = false,\r\n        },\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlthough in your case you seem to use 'ray-x/go.nvim', in which case there is [a separate way to configure LSP server](https://github.com/ray-x/go.nvim?tab=readme-ov-file#lsp). So I'd say it would be something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('go').setup({\r\n  lsp_cfg = {\r\n    capabilities = {\r\n      textDocument = {\r\n        completion = {\r\n          completionItem = {\r\n            snippetSupport = false,\r\n          },\r\n        },\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```",
