            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I don't know if this will be useful to anyone else but I had a similar issue and ended up writing a little hack that just always tries to expand the inserted text (which just does nothing if the text does not include any snippet placeholders). I'm using `vim.snippet.expand` which requires neovim 0.11, but you can replace it with any other engine for expanding the snippets.\n```lua\n-- autoexpand.lua\n\nlocal clear_text = function (r1, c1, r2, c2)\n\tvim.api.nvim_buf_set_text(0, r1, c1, r2, c2, {})\nend\n\nlocal get_line = function (row)\n\treturn vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, row, row + 1, false)[1]\nend\n\nlocal remove_inserted_text = function (txt)\n\tlocal cursor = vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)\n\tlocal row, col = cursor[1] - 1, cursor[2]\n\tlocal _, num_extra_lines = txt:gsub(\"\\n\", \"\\n\")\n\tif num_extra_lines == 0 then\n\t\tclear_text(row, col - txt:len(), row, col)\n\t\treturn\n\tend\n\tlocal start_row = row - num_extra_lines\n\tlocal buf_line1 = get_line(start_row)\n\tlocal txt_line1 = txt:match(\"^[^\\n]*\")\n\tlocal start_col = buf_line1:len() - txt_line1:len()\n\tclear_text(start_row, start_col, row, col)\nend\n\nlocal expand_lsp_snippet = function()\n\tlocal path = { \"user_data\", \"nvim\", \"lsp\", \"completion_item\" }\n\tlocal item = vim.tbl_get(vim.v.completed_item, unpack(path))\n\tlocal txt = vim.tbl_get(item or {}, \"insertText\")\n\tlocal fmt = vim.tbl_get(item or {}, \"insertTextFormat\")\n\tif fmt ~= 2 or txt == 0 then return end\n\tremove_inserted_text(txt)\n\tvim.snippet.expand(txt)\nend\n\nlocal setup = function ()\n\tvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"CompleteDone\", {\n\t\tcallback = expand_lsp_snippet,\n\t})\nend\n\nreturn { setup = setup }\n```\nI never wrote any lua before this so I'm sure this code is awful and has lots of bugs, but so far it's been working great for me so maybe someone will find it useful :smile:\n\nEdit:\nI just realized that with this hack I can now support snippets provided by the LSP by just changing this one line in `process_items`:\n```diff\nprocess_items = function(items, base)\n\tlocal res = vim.tbl_filter(function(item)\n\t\t-- Keep items which match the base and are not snippets\n\t\tlocal text = item.filterText or H.get_completion_word(item)\n-\t\treturn vim.startswith(text, base) and item.kind ~= 15\n+\t\treturn vim.startswith(text, base)\n\tend, items)\n\n\tres = vim.deepcopy(res)\n\ttable.sort(res, function(a, b) return (a.sortText or a.label) < (b.sortText or b.label) end)\n\n\t-- Possibly add \"kind\" highlighting\n\tif _G.MiniIcons ~= nil then\n\t\tlocal add_kind_hlgroup = H.make_add_kind_hlgroup()\n\t\tfor _, item in ipairs(res) do\n\t\t\tadd_kind_hlgroup(item)\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\n\treturn res\nend\n```\nI'm not sure how to do this without modifying the plugin code because I can't just copy it into the config since it uses `H` which is not exported.",
